Conventions summary:
This is the Pallets Click repository, a Python project organized in a src-based 
layout with its package code under src/, tests under tests/, documentation under
docs/, and additional usage samples under examples/. It uses uv for dependency 
management and environment setup, so you should use uv rather than pip when 
installing requirements locally. The test suite is run with pytest, and code 
style is enforced by ruff, which acts as both the formatter and the linter; run 
ruff checks on your changes before committing. Continuous integration is handled
via GitHub Actions, though the specific workflow details were not examined 
beyond the presence of workflow files. Any other contributor requirements, such 
as commit-message conventions or additional build steps, were not detected.

